    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What I implemented\n\n`namesakeCount` \u2014 for each newly created owner, the number of owners that already existed sharing the same `firstName` **and** `lastName`, compared case-insensitively \u2014 is now computed at create time, persisted, and returned on the owner representation.\n\n## Changes\n\n1. **`ClinicServiceImpl.createOwner`** \u2014 computes and stamps the count before persisting, so it never counts the owner itself. Added a small single-responsibility helper `countNamesakes(Owner)` that reuses the existing `OwnerRepository.findByLastNameIgnoreCase` query (already used by the household check) and filters by case-insensitive first name. No new repository method or code duplication.\n\n2. **`Owner` model** \u2014 new persisted `namesake_count` column (`Integer namesakeCount`) with getter/setter, matching the existing pattern for `customerCode`/`householdId`.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `namesakeCount` integer to the `Owner` schema. The DTO is generated from this at build time, and MapStruct maps it automatically by name (no mapper edits needed).\n\n4. **DB schemas** \u2014 added `namesake_count INTEGER` to all four (`h2`, `hsqldb`, `mysql`, `postgres`) for consistency.\n\nThe `coreCountsNamesakes` acceptance test (two owners sharing name but differing address \u2192 second reports `namesakeCount = 1`) passes, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
